title: Pressing Buttons
files:
  - em.prog:em.examples.basic/Ex07_Button3P.em.ts
  - em.core:em.hal/ButtonI.em.ts
  - rpi.2040:rpi.distro.2040/BoardC.em.ts
  - em.core:em.utils/ButtonT.em.ts
  - .assets/img-101-10-01.png

steps:
  - cmds:
      - view 5
    text: |

      {[ht,$start]&thinsp; Pressing Buttons}

      This tour examines {[cu]Button3P}, which uses a **del&shy;egate** implementing a higher-level {[cu]ButtonI} **interface**.

      This program can discriminate between different kinds of button presses, based upon their duration:

      {[bm,1]} a _glitch_ press, falling below a minimum duration<br>
      {[bm,2]} a _short_ press, exceding a minimum duration<br>
      {[bm,3]} a _long_ press, exceding a maximum duration

      In the case of {[cu]Button3P}, short [100&thinsp;ms] and long [4&thinsp;s] presses will respectively wink `AppLed` and `SysLed`.

  - cmds:
      - open 1
      - mark 1 A 7
      - mark 1 B 14
      - mark 1 C 20
    focus: [1, 1]
    acts: [$reveal, $build]
    text: |

      {[ht,$details]&thinsp; %[cu]Button3P% &ndash; Details}

      <div class="em-bmlist">

      {[bm,A]} {[cu]Button3P} uses an {[cu]AppBut} **delegate** exported by the current {[cu]BoardC} &emsp; <span class="em codicon codicon-circuit-board"></span>&thinsp;**composite**.<br>

      {[bm,B]} {[cu]AppBut}.{[cf]onPressed} [**`targ`**] binds a local event hand&shy;ler and specifies the [&thinsp;<b>t</b><sup>min</sup>, <b>t</b><sup>max</sup>&thinsp;] press durations.

      {[bm,C]} {[cu]AppBut}.{[cf]isPressed} tests if this event corresponds to a _long_ press exceeding <b>t</b><sup>max</sup>.

      </div>

      {[cu]AppBut} will _not_ invoke the {[cf]onPressedH} hand&shy;ler if a 1&thinsp;&rarr;&thinsp;0&thinsp;&rarr;&thinsp;1 pulse on the `AppBut` pin doesn't cross  <b>t</b><sup>min</sup>.

      The {[cu]AppBut} **delegate** does invoke {[cf]onPressedH} when the `AppBut` pin returns to 1 _or else_ remains 0 after <b>t</b><sup>max</sup>.

  - cmds:
      - open 2
    focus: [2, 1]
    acts: [$reveal]
    text: |

      {[ht,$peek]&thinsp; %[cu]ButtonI% &ndash; Quick Look}

      Reading the {[cu]ButtonI} **interface** should seem second nature to you by now.

      As you'll see, our {[cu]AppBut} **delegate** &ndash; which imple&shy;ments this **interface** &ndash; originates as a {[cu]ButtonT} **template** clone.

  - cmds:
      - open 4
      - mark 4 A 12
      - mark 4 B 16
      - mark 4 C 19
      - mark 4 D 27
      - mark 4 E 32
      - mark 4 F 37
    focus: [4, 9]
    acts: [$reveal]
    text: |

      {[ht,$details]&thinsp; %[cu]ButtonT% &ndash; Details}

      The **module** cloned via {[cu]ButtonT} employs a design not unlike the {[cu]Button2} program of the prior tour:

      {[bm,A]}We use an {[cu]EdgeI} **proxy** (not a named **delegate**).<br>
      {[bm,B]}We use an internal {[ct]Fiber} to debounce (not blink).<br>
      {[bm,C]}We bind callback functions at build-time [**`meta`**].<br>
      {[bm,D]}We track the "press" state at run-time [**`targ`**].<br>
      {[bm,E]}We setup edge detection during {[cs]em$startup}.<br>
      {[bm,F]}We (conditionally) {[cf]post} our {[ct]Fiber} upon detection.<br>

      We further classify the kind of button press &ndash; _glitch_, _short_, _long_ &ndash; using the state variables declared at {[bm,D]}.

  - cmds:
      - open 4
      - mark 4 A 12
      - mark 4 B 16
      - mark 4 C 19
      - mark 4 D 27
      - mark 4 E 32
      - mark 4 F 37

      - mark 4 G 45
      - mark 4 H 54
      - mark 4 I 65

    focus: [4, 45]
    acts: [$reveal]
    text: |

      {[ht,$details]&thinsp; %[cu]ButtonT% &ndash; More Details}

      When dispatched, {[cf]debounceFB} uses the {[cu]Poller} **module** at {[bm,G]} to iteratively await passage of {[cn]cur_min} msecs.

      {[bi,arrow_circle_right]} If not pressed after the first pause, we have a _glitch_.<br>
      {[bi,arrow_circle_right]} Update {[cn]cur_dur} and test for a _short_ or _long_ press.<br>
      {[bi,arrow_circle_right]} Call {[cf]cur_fxn} [{[ct]Handler}] after exiting this loop.

      The {[cf]isPressed} function at {[bm,H]} defers to the state of the {[cn]Edge} **proxy** &ndash; assuming `AppBut` tests active-low.

      After initializing the tracking variables, the {[cf]onPressed} function at {[bm,I]} conditionally enables edge detection.

  - cmds:
      - open 3
      - mark 3 A 26
      - mark 3 B 59
    focus: [3, 30]
    acts: [$reveal]
    text: |

      {[ht,$peek]&thinsp; %[cu]BoardC% &ndash; A Look Back}

      In case you don't notice on earlier visits, {[cu]BoardC} first clones {[cu]ButtonT} into the {[cu]AppBut} **delegate**  at {[bm,A]}.

      {[cu]BoardC} at {[bm,B]} then binds the {[cu]AppButEdge} **delegate** (also cloned above) to the {[cu]AppBut}.{[cn]Edge} **proxy**.

  - cmds:
      - open 4
    focus: [4, 45]
    text: |

      {[ht,$extra]&thinsp;Extra Credit}

      {[bi,task_alt]} Quantify the {[cf]debounceFB} overhead at _run-time_.

      {[bi,task_alt]} Would a _build-time_ {[cf]onPressed} save time&thinsp;&middot;&thinsp;space.

      {[bi,task_alt]} Generalize {[cu]ButtonT} to handle active-high buttons.

  - cmds:
      - view 5
    text: |

      {[ht,$steps]&thinsp;Next Steps}

      Congratulations&thinsp;&hellip;&nbsp; You've completed the last tour with&shy;in the **Basic Examples** series 🎉.

      You now have a working knowledge of **EMS** as well as exper&shy;ience using core **EM&bull;porium** content.

      Check back regularly, as more tours come online cover&shy;ing high-level as well as low-level aspects of **EMS**.

      {[hc]}
